---
/**
 * About page — practice positioning, services, bio, contact.
 *
 * Sections (anchor IDs):
 *   #hero     — h1 + lede + headshot + primary CTA
 *   #services — h2, two service offerings (AT Consulting + Public Speaking)
 *   #bio      — h2, longer about-the-practice paragraph
 *   #contact  — h2, mailto link
 *
 * Heading hierarchy: one h1, h2 per section, h3 for service blocks.
 *
 * This page absorbed the original /index.astro after the 2026-05-21 pivot
 * to a blog-first homepage. /about/ remains the canonical place to learn
 * what Mountain Dog Consulting does and how to hire.
 */
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import portraitSrc from '../assets/taylor-portrait.png';

const title = 'About — Mountain Dog Consulting';
const description = 'Taylor Danielson — assistive technology consultant in British Columbia. Assistive robotics, environmental control, and smart-home integration, from years of daily use.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} onAboutPage={true}>
  <section id="hero" class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
    <div class="hero__inner">
      <div class="hero__copy">
        <h1 id="hero-heading">Assistive technology that works in real life.</h1>
        <p class="hero__lede">
          I'm Taylor Danielson, an assistive technology consultant based in British
          Columbia. I work on assistive robotics, environmental control, and
          smart-home integration — and on the harder problem of making any of it
          actually fit the person who has to live with it.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="#contact" class="button">Get in touch</a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero__portrait">
        <Picture
          src={portraitSrc}
          formats={['avif', 'webp']}
          fallbackFormat="jpg"
          widths={[400, 600, 800]}
          sizes="(max-width: 50rem) 80vw, 22rem"
          quality={{ avif: 60, webp: 80, jpg: 82 }}
          alt="Taylor Danielson, smiling, in a power wheelchair, wearing a Technology for Living vest."
          priority
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="work" aria-labelledby="work-heading" class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__inner">
      <h2 id="work-heading">What I do</h2>
      <p>
        The hard part of assistive technology is rarely the spec sheet. It's
        matching the right tools to the right person, in the space the technology
        has to live in, with a plan the people doing the work can actually follow.
        At the centre of the practice is one question: what would it take for this
        technology to actually work for the person using it?
      </p>
      <p>
        That question covers a lot of ground. Over five years, Mountain Dog has
        taken on assistive-robotics user experience, editorial and program work
        for disability nonprofits, custom builds for grant administration and
        similar back-office systems, accessibility audits, board work in the
        disability sector, and occasional speaking. The shape varies; the question
        doesn't.
      </p>
      <p>
        Behind all of this is more than two decades of using assistive technology
        as a person with a physical disability, plus formal experience in
        nonprofit operations, board governance, and accessibility consulting.
        Some of the same iterations show up on the <a href="/">blog</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        New engagements are selective — the calendar usually has steady work —
        but if you have something where you think there might be a fit, please
        <a href="#contact">reach out</a>. I'd rather hear about it and figure out
        together whether it's the right match than have you assume it isn't.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-heading" class="section">
    <div class="section__inner">
      <h2 id="contact-heading">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        The fastest way to reach me is by email. I read everything that comes in and
        reply within two business days; if your message is time-sensitive, mention that
        in the subject line.
      </p>
      <p class="contact__mailto">
        <a href="mailto:taylor@mountaindogconsulting.com" class="button">
          Email taylor@mountaindogconsulting.com
        </a>
      </p>
      <p>
        For accessibility feedback about this site specifically, please write to
        <a href="mailto:accessibility@mountaindogconsulting.com">
          accessibility@mountaindogconsulting.com
        </a>. See also the <a href="/accessibility/">accessibility statement</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
